content.text:
In Tailwind v4 (CSS-first config), use the `@custom-variant` directive in your CSS instead of `tailwind.config.js`:

```css
@custom-variant pwa (&:where(@media (display-mode: standalone)));
```

Actually for a media query, use the shorthand:

```css
@custom-variant pwa (@media (display-mode: standalone));
```

Then use it like any built-in variant: `<button className="mb-2 md:mb-4 pwa:mb-6" />`

**Source:** `src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx`, "Adding custom variants" section (~line 672-708), which shows the `@custom-variant` directive with both nested and shorthand syntax (e.g. `@custom-variant theme-midnight (&:where(...))` and a media-query-nested example with `any-hover`).

